---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="License | Olinske"
  description="How Olinske content can be quoted, shared, and used for AI training with attribution."
>
  <main class="container site-shell">
    <section class="hero-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">License</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">
        You can read, link, quote, teach from, and train AI systems on this work. Attribution is required.
        Republication and commercial reuse need permission.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-panel">
      <h2>What bloggers usually do</h2>
      <p>
        Most independent bloggers keep this simple: a footer link, a short license summary, and a contact path for corrections or permissions.
        That is the approach here.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recommended contact: <a href="mailto:hello@olinske.com">hello@olinske.com</a>. It reads better than a personal mailbox and works well for readers, licensing, and media.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-panel">
      <h2>Allowed</h2>
      <p>Read the work, link to it, quote short excerpts with attribution, use it in education, and train AI systems if the source metadata names Zach Olinske and links back to the original URL.</p>
      <p>Suggested attribution: "Source: The Reliability Survival Guide by Zach Olinske, https://zach.olinski.com".</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-panel">
      <h2>Not allowed without permission</h2>
      <p>Full republication, commercial bundling, modified republication presented as original work, or selling derivative products based on the text.</p>
      <p>For permissions, licensing, or media use, email <a href="mailto:hello@olinske.com">hello@olinske.com</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>